## 6. Explanation of Important HTML Elements

1. `<header>`: Displays the website title and introductory text.
2. `<nav>`: Contains navigation links to different pages or sections.
3. `<main>`: Contains the main content of the webpage.
4. `<section>`: Groups related content, such as About Me and Skills.
5. `<article>`: Displays individual projects independently.
6. `<img>`: Displays images on the webpage.
7. `alt`: Provides meaningful alternative text for images.
8. `<ul>` and `<li>`: Display skills, interests, and technologies as lists.
9. `<a>`: Creates links to other pages, external resources, and email addresses.
10. `<footer>`: Displays copyright and contact information.

## 7. How to Run the Project

1. Open Visual Studio Code.
2. Create a folder named `portfolio-project`.
